# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Editor / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Claude Code local config ---
.claude/

# --- Session captures and generated artefacts ---
# data/ holds .npz session files, exported xlsx, plot folders, ML
# models — none of that belongs in the source tree. If you need a
# small sample to ship, force-add it explicitly with `git add -f`.
data/
*.npz
*.pkl
*.xlsx
*.tif
*.svg
*_plots/
qinj_dataset.csv
# Canonical local bench-test session directory per CLAUDE.md §9.
# Holds .npz / .txt / .xlsx / .tif / .svg per-run output AND the
# project-tree-preferred crash log paths (pulsar_*.log).  None of
# this is source — it's user data + post-mortem diagnostics that
# accumulate as the operator runs experiments.
test/

# --- Installer build outputs ---
installer/build/
installer/dist/
installer/Output/
*.exe

# --- Reference scope manual dumps ---
# Leave these out of git — they're 1 MB+ of static reference text
# pulled from the Tek manual. Keep locally for offline lookup.
tbs_full.txt
TBS2000B_manual.txt

# --- Scratch / debug artefacts at the repo root ---
# Local-only test scripts (proper tests go in tests/), debug PNGs
# from one-off analyses, ad-hoc stdout/stderr captures.  These
# accumulate during interactive bench debugging; the canonical
# version of anything useful ends up in tests/ or in a docstring.
# Patterns deliberately scoped to the ROOT (leading slash) so they
# don't shadow legitimate files deeper in the tree (e.g.
# tests/test_*.py).
/test_*.py
/*.png
/*.log
/out*.txt
/gui_*.txt
/gui_*.log
# Per-launch diagnostic written by PULSAR.vbs (see CLAUDE.md §9,
# gotcha #14).  Overwritten on every launch; not source.
/pulsar_launcher.log
/pulsar_launch_error.log
/pulsar_faulthandler.log

# --- Email / SMTP secrets ---
# Belt-and-braces — the config path is in $HOME, but if anyone ever
# drops one here by mistake, don't push it.
email_config.json
.stimtest/

# --- Local-only planning / private docs ---
# CLAUDE.md is the AI-agent project memory (auto-loaded by Claude
# Code from the project root).  It accumulates design notes,
# gotchas, and ongoing-work context — including collaborator-only
# (CWRU) material that should NOT be on GitHub.  The repo already
# lives in OneDrive (C:\Users\chris\OneDrive\GitHub\…), so the file
# is automatically backed up via OneDrive sync; gitignore just
# prevents accidental `git add` from pushing it.
#
# EXTENSION_PLUGIN_DESIGN.md is the design doc for the
# stimtest_cwru extension refactor — same confidentiality reason.
#
# Future agents: if you write a new design / planning markdown that
# mentions the CWRU profile or any collaborator-only feature, add
# it to this section too.  Public-facing docs (README.md,
# CHANGELOG.md, docstrings) stay tracked as normal.
CLAUDE.md
EXTENSION_PLUGIN_DESIGN.md
# LOG_ANALYSIS.md is the rolling log-file findings report — kept
# private so internal observations about bench-session glitches,
# perf hot-spots, and recurring errors don't ship to GitHub.
# Findings here either get distilled into CLAUDE.md gotchas (when
# the fix lands) or into task-tracker items (for unresolved bugs).
# See "Performance / log monitoring discipline" in CLAUDE.md.
LOG_ANALYSIS.md
# Defensive: if someone scaffolds the CWRU extension as a
# subdirectory of THIS repo instead of as a sibling (per the design
# doc §3), don't push it.  The extension is meant to live in its
# own private repo, not this one.
stimtest_cwru/
stimtest_*/

# Collaborator login profiles bundled into the installer.  These are
# CWRU-specific data artifacts (login name + SHA-256 password hash +
# unlocked shape IDs) — distributed out-of-band to collaborators, never
# published in the public PULSAR repo (same confidentiality rule as the
# stimtest_cwru extension above).  They live locally so the operator's
# ``installer/build.py`` bundles them, but they're not committed; the
# .iss entry uses ``skipifsourcedoesntexist`` so a public-repo build
# still succeeds without them.
installer/profiles/

# Claude Code scratch/working files (never commit)
.claude-tmp/
